<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title><%= for_parent? ? "Get started" : "Sign in" %> - Remindly</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <style><%= render partial: "shared/ui_styles", formats: :css %></style>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-gray-50">
    <div class="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-md w-full space-y-8">
        <%# Most people arrive here from Sign in on the public site. Without
            this, the only way back was the How to page. %>
        <div class="text-center">
          <%= link_to "← Back to the Remindly home page", root_path, class: "text-sm font-medium text-blue-700 hover:underline" %>
        </div>

        <%#
          This page is where a new account starts as well as where an old one
          signs in, and it used to read only as the second: "Remindly Caregiver
          Dashboard", "Sign in with your email", "Send Magic Link". Somebody who
          had just pressed "Set up reminders for my parent" saw a log-in screen
          and assumed they needed an account first.

          So the visitor who came from that button is greeted with what they
          asked for, and everyone else is told the same link creates an account.
          The button says what it does in plain words; "magic link" means nothing
          to someone who has never had one.
        %>
        <div>
          <h1 class="mt-6 text-center text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900">
            <%= for_parent? ? "Start setting up reminders for your parent" : "Sign in to Remindly" %>
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-3 text-center text-gray-600">
            <% if for_parent? %>
              <strong>New here? This creates your account.</strong> Free, and no password.
            <% else %>
              <strong>New here?</strong> The same link creates your account. Free, and no password.
            <% end %>
          </p>
        </div>

        <% if flash[:notice] %>
          <div class="bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-400 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-green-700"><%= flash[:notice] %></p>
          </div>
        <% end %>

        <% if flash[:alert] %>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-400 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-red-700"><%= flash[:alert] %></p>
          </div>
        <% end %>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
          <%= form_with url: request_magic_link_path, method: :post, class: "space-y-6" do |f| %>
            <%= hidden_field_tag :for, "parent" if for_parent? %>
            <%= hidden_field_tag :from, campaign_source if campaign_source %>
            <div>
              <%= f.label :email, "Your email address", class: "block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700" %>
              <%= f.email_field :email, required: true, autofocus: true, autocomplete: "email", placeholder: "you@example.com", class: "field mt-1 block w-full" %>
            </div>

            <div>
              <%= f.submit "Email me a secure sign-in link", class: "button button-primary group relative w-full flex" %>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-900">What happens next</p>
            <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal list-inside space-y-1 text-sm text-blue-800">
              <li>We email you a link. Open it and you're in. The link expires after 30 minutes; if it does, just ask for a new one here.</li>
              <% if for_parent? %>
                <li>Add your parent: their name and timezone. They need no email, password or account.</li>
                <li>Write their first reminder. No reminder reaches them until they agree; the first call or screen only asks.</li>
              <% else %>
                <li>If you're new, say whether you're setting Remindly up for someone or receiving the reminders yourself, and you're in.</li>
              <% end %>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray-600">
            Want to see it first? <%= link_to "How Remindly works", how_to_path, class: "font-medium text-blue-700 hover:underline" %>
          </p>

          <% if Rails.env.development? %>
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center">
                <div class="w-full border-t border-gray-300"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="relative flex justify-center text-sm">
                <span class="px-2 bg-gray-50 text-gray-500">Or use dev mode</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-md shadow-sm space-y-2">
              <%# By role, not by address. These used to pass caregiver@example.com
                  and senior@example.com, and both of those accounts hold the
                  opposite role to their name — so each button signed you in as
                  the thing the other one promised. %>
              <%= link_to "Quick Login as Caregiver", dev_login_path(role: "caregiver"), class: "button button-secondary group relative w-full flex" %>
              <%= link_to "Quick Login as Care Receiver", dev_login_path(role: "senior"), class: "button button-secondary group relative w-full flex" %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>

        <!-- Version Info -->
        <div class="mt-4 text-center">
          <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">v<%= APP_VERSION %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
